{title: Pass Me Not, O Gentle Savior}
{artist: Fanny Crosby & William Doane}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
[G]Pass me not, O [C]gentle [G]Savior — hear my humble [D]cry;
[G]while on others [C]thou art [G]calling, [D]do not pass me [G]by.

Chorus
[G]Savior, [C]Savior, [G]hear my humble [D]cry;
[G]while on others [C]thou art [G]calling, [D]do not pass me [G]by.

Verse 2
[G]Let me at Thy throne of mercy [C]Find [G]a sweet relief, Kneeling there in deep contrition; [D]Help my
[G]unbelief. Savior, Savior, Hear my [C]humble cry; While [G]on others [D]Thou art calling, Do not pass [G]me by.

Verse 3
[G]3, Trusting only in Thy merit, Would [C]I seek [G]Thy face; Heal my wounded, broken spirit, Save [D]me by
[G]Thy grace. Savior, Savior, Hear [C]my humble cry; While [G]on [D]others Thou art calling, Do not pass [G]me by.

Verse 4
[G]Thou the Spring of all my comfort, More [C]than life [G]to me, Whom have I on earth beside Thee? [D]Whom in
[G]Heav'n but Thee? Savior, Savior, [C]Hear my humble cry; [G]While on [D]others Thou art calling, Do not pass [G]me by.
